<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Adil Shah I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1580</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> I was the fifth Adil Shahi sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, ruling from 1558 to 1580. He joined the alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> that crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talikota">Battle of Talikota</a> in 1565, but his long siege of Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> in 1570–1571 failed. He completed the walls of Bijapur, began its great Jama Masjid, and was murdered in 1580.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-adil-shah-i.jpg" alt="Ali Adil Shah I" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aliadilshah.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
